\newlabel{fig:c26-rmqfig}{{9.3.1}{561}{The reduction on $A=(3,1,4,2)$: to find $\min \{a_1,a_2,a_3\}$ read the two endpoint nodes $1$ and $3$ (ringed), climb to their lowest common ancestor -- node $2$ -- and take its value, $1$. That is $\thmref {c26-rmqlca}$; the dashed paths are the way up to the shared ancestor}{figure.caption.97}{}}
